{"title":"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Diophantine_PoP)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Diophantine PoP)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3df79a4384bc29acd37e14b0430773d09964ddd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup ABC$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/c/aac3ee19b22616068ded3a68e1204ab73ef7f670.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 86$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/6/0a6ad94dd4e8984e88a1e416355c6a7d5fcabeb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 97$\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />. A circle with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Moreover <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/e/40e341674d6c973ae0dd53dace5036995f31997b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BX}$\" width=\"31\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/9/5895bfa441a2027d808cec50fa4da5229e07e89e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CX}$\" width=\"31\" height=\"15\" /> have integer lengths. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/1/471420da4ee16be0678246cb886486cd1448ffab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} \\ 11 \\qquad  \\textbf{(B)} \\ 28 \\qquad  \\textbf{(C)} \\ 33 \\qquad  \\textbf{(D)} \\ 61 \\qquad  \\textbf{(E)} \\ 72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Diophantine_PoP.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Diophantine_PoP)\">Solution 1 (Diophantine PoP)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Diophantine PoP)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/c/77ce7565827bb55748707258399412ab0383d8b9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] //Made by samrocksnature size(8cm); pair A,B,C,D,E,X; A=(0,0); B=(-53.4,-67.4); C=(0,-97); D=(0,-86); E=(0,86); X=(-29,-81); draw(circle(A,86)); draw(E--C--B--A--X); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,NE); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,S); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,NE); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,NE); label(&quot;$X$&quot;,X,dir(250)); dot(A^^B^^C^^D^^E^^X); [/asy]\" width=\"318\" height=\"378\" />\n</p><p>Let circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> as shown. We apply Power of a Point on point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with respect to circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/8207b79435a4bd499da7598fb44424c8a8499238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> This yields the diophantine equation \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/5/6955597337bfaf1bbd79dd1d15d2ba9d9227b592.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CX \\cdot CB = CD \\cdot CE\\]\" width=\"168\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/4/dc4add72db43218e0aa56ac52e01618be9434f5a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CX(CX+XB) = (97-86)(97+86)\\]\" width=\"296\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/4/0645db9f2cad48e2fafc2d537016066c30a8b241.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CX(CX+XB) = 3 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 61.\\]\" width=\"228\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since lengths cannot be negative, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/9/b09b0d7c988db29e9a08901cd69593488a5a9e99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CX+XB \\ge CX.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"145\" height=\"17\" /> This generates the four solution pairs for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/b/b0bc80da9fe0beb4faaef634cc81f7316f6cd707.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(CX,CX+XB)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"138\" height=\"20\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/c/6ecaeb68a9caf2a965d78622451d2ee3774faa96.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(1,2013) \\qquad (3,671) \\qquad (11,183) \\qquad (33,61).\\]\" width=\"353\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>However, by the Triangle Inequality on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/6/576d27297ff8bebed39327fe4a334b9f91f52027.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACX,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" /> we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/4/294d2de3cd8e802e2d99551b68c3033d65ddb4a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CX&gt;13.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" /> This implies that we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/9/3d9004ee1b9554d4e52c82782d16333b0eab9347.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CX+XB= \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }61}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"181\" height=\"30\" /> \n</p><p>(Solution by unknown, latex/asy modified majorly by samrocksnature)\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/d/3bd0d1ded44edd12c5c2ea6290b65bde3a31d2eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX = q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d57a7d3459de8353ddcb527dc4c2038902d3154.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CX = p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> meet the circle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/7370a7b3a820622f89dcd80da5b19d135ce9175c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AZ = AY = 86$\" width=\"121\" height=\"13\" />.  Using the Power of a Point, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f83e04c3156ab3b3d2d1ac7d487638b652f4c53c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(p+q) = 11(183) = 11 * 3 * 61$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"251\" height=\"18\" />.  We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/c/65cfdc5838fc3c6d839488e35ee13f03dc88c381.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q&gt;p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/9/1792efa42bbaf227ee6321a141bfe7d0d0072e0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p&gt;13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> by the triangle inequality on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af253e8b1b795df12f128aad8ff98d491a56fad6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />.  Thus, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/e/c5e142c28844cf10740ca4a7d9715b407c83deff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = p+q = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }61}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"183\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> represent <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/73205379672e860eb250c541187600fae3a3e225.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CX$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> represent <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a4b9c32938e96f30b59dcb29f410cd4c2e3982.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" />. Since the circle goes through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/d/32d67201d74984f4154c1626066765c65897e0cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AX = 86$\" width=\"124\" height=\"13\" />.\nThen by Stewart's Theorem,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/e/afe154b646e779e9d2ac9b3ecbe3b7dc1547c895.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy(x+y) + 86^2 (x+y) = 97^2 y + 86^2 x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"305\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/7/957fa992e71cfcdc396697aeca7de7e2ccb9c010.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 y + xy^2 + 86^2 x + 86^2 y = 97^2 y + 86^2 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"310\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/9/529687b2555be9f749b13c3f315b253698eeb9e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + xy + 86^2 = 97^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> cannot be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, dividing both sides of the equation by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is allowed.)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ec82cd8d508332b558536634b6cd65d7444d5ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x+y) = (97+86)(97-86)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"234\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/5/f35141eea0a87f64f3789125ead69c396b347d8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x+y) = 2013$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>The prime factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa725c98dfe19f98809033755b801810bc298aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2013$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/866b44935f69a5b800547127fe13210bb1e36fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$61$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />. Obviously, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/1/3b12e98e20610031ffc93c31267bc4689c6c2bfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" />. In addition, by the Triangle Inequality, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/3/c5393cb3cdb1294a26e5901968bf388393de0c35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC &lt; AB + AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/9/7f91fb98d0e5e33bf3190d5f6e5b38f5e904f690.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y &lt; 183$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f3bccae16d5e31266370fced24edc41538d5da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/d/d3da9f8c7fe0473fdd6f8597eff61d71fedda430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> must equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/1/2514598e8f3dc38f9a9a05a7aea48ff619e29537.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }61}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Motivation and general line of reasoning: we use a law of cosines condition on triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/5/c25098016dac91dc30e5febffb0d0e73a92f96e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABX$\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> and triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> to derive some equivalent formations of the same quantity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/c/1dc0f84230d6166da3a17d8ebfdb5d0178da2c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos B$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, which looks promising since it involves the desired length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, as well as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a4b9c32938e96f30b59dcb29f410cd4c2e3982.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/73205379672e860eb250c541187600fae3a3e225.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CX$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" />.An intermediate step would be to use the integer condition and pay attention to the divisors of stuff. \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a4b9c32938e96f30b59dcb29f410cd4c2e3982.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" />=<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/73205379672e860eb250c541187600fae3a3e225.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CX$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" />=<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7d010bbff66a0c41e43310a51efbaa6bf63396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />. \n</p><p>First we have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/2/622c9de1ab4165061cc530415b636aa41e25de65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(B)=\\frac{86^2+x_{1}^2-86^2}{172x_{1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"197\" height=\"44\" /> \nby applying the law of cosines to triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/5/c25098016dac91dc30e5febffb0d0e73a92f96e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABX$\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />. Another equivalent formation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/c/1dc0f84230d6166da3a17d8ebfdb5d0178da2c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos B$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/a/6aab3a956748e99479f0c24d347bb5b25cd75f84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{86^2+(x_{1}+x_2)^2-97^2}{172(x_{1}+x_2)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"181\" height=\"45\" />. \nNow that we have the necessary ingredients, we can make a system of equations and deduce that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/a/9ba6558073c93e30ffec3ca406b9b633eac5450f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1=\\frac{(x_1+x_2)^2+86^2-97^2}{x_1+x_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"223\" height=\"44\" />. \n</p><p>Don't lose focus by now-we try to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/c/87cf8bc498151d722a3b34591ca7468d43e95939.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1+x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />, an integer value as given in the problem. To do this, we want the quantity \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/f/d8ff9b536b58361312662e71b3bde4df6acb6c93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(x_1+x_2)^2+86^2-97^2}{x_1+x_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"181\" height=\"44\" /> \nto 1) be an integer and 2) smaller than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/c/87cf8bc498151d722a3b34591ca7468d43e95939.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1+x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />. For the sake of conciseness in notation we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/1/c115e56c25d3afd28bb1ded83db6760d4bed4882.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M=x_1+x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"17\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/e/dfefb8988bad2dab7f8d9c3d71860ef5168865cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M+\\frac{86^2-97^2}{M}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"121\" height=\"41\" /> is an integer. Now recalling the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7a54d6857592c5ce4ac8c2a7435d79f4840c3f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b)(a-b)=a^2-b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"185\" height=\"19\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/9/db9de9bbf6b4db80d45a934d44e56e23e9c41411.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{183(-11)}{M}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"80\" height=\"40\" /> must be an integer.\n</p><p>Now the prime factor decomposition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/e/ace09fdb5b39502c9d5b20472538801a68dbeac7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$183 \\cdot -11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" /> is  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/2/2127e7a25ea7308037b6bae51d497adb978a813d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(61)(3)(-11)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" />. Trying out all the possible integer values that divide this quantity, we get that the only viable option for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is 61 (verify that yourself!) Therefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/1/2514598e8f3dc38f9a9a05a7aea48ff619e29537.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }61}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" />. (Solution by CreamyCream123)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2013amc12a/357\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2013amc12a/357</a>\n</p><p>~dolphin7\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zxW3uvCQFls\">https://youtu.be/zxW3uvCQFls</a>\n</p><p>~sugar_rush\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A\">2013 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?t